  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1244 PM MDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nSaturday...Another cool front comes down in the morning. Max temp \nwill fall down into the mid to upper 80s across the plains and \nvalleys. As for precip, mainly isolated pops across the higher \nterrain with one or two showers pushing onto the I-25 corridor during \nthe early evening.\n\nSunday, southwesterly flow throughout the column increases. However, \nmonsoon moisture will be entrained into this flow. Likewise, pops \nwill increase over the mtns (especially the divide) and temps on the \nplains will rise well into the 90s. One or two storms will be \npossibe along a lee trough extending from the Kim to Lamar region. \nAnother area of showers may be possible over the lower elevations of \nthe Pikes Peak region. \n\nFor Monday, moist southwesterly flow continues across the region. \nTemps will be a few degrees cooler and there will be a better chance \nof showers and storms across all of the region.\n\nTuesday things get interesting. Statistical guidance along with \ndeterministic guidance shows the potential for a wetter and much \ncooler temps to move into the region. However, there is not \nunanimous agreement as there is a large range showing up within the \nmax temps data for this day (although the overall trend is much \ncooler). Additionally, the monsoonal moisture will blend in with the \nmoisture aloft, and this could lead to a much wetter pattern.\n\nThis overall cooler/wetter pattern will last into late week \nnext week, so we will likely see the potential for a cooler and \nwetter pattern from the Tuesday through Thursday time frame. \n\\/Hodanish",
